[17592186401192 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401192 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "14c27fbe-cfe3-5924-a55c-3737ccd260a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402616 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402617 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402616 #edb/ref 1069 "q-38245" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402616 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402616 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}+{v}^{2} \\\\ {u}^{2}-{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402616 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "48feab89-768b-5b8e-8c0a-02f86fdff070" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402616 #edb/ref 1074 "Given a transformation \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the locations of the critical points of $T,$ we need to solve \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x(u,v)={u}^{2}+{v}^{2}$ and $y(u,v)={u}^{2}-{v}^{2}.$ \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =2v \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =2u & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =-2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2u & 2v \\\\ 2u & -2v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2u\\cdot (-2v)-2v\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =-4uv-4uv \\\\  & =-8uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =0 \\\\ -8uv & =0 \\\\ uv & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $uv=0$ defines the pair of intersecting lines $u=0$ and $v=0$ in the $uv$-plane. Notice that these lines correspond to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402617 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402617 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402619 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402617 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402617 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402617 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402617 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402617 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402617 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186402620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402617 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f05d1ca1-306f-5d0c-970a-e108a73f246e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402618 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical points lie on the lines $u+v=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402618 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402618 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9d467be4-da9c-5949-964e-fc1ece22124b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402619 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical points lie on the line $u-v=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402619 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402619 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "99d8765a-e6b9-5b6f-b95c-7ee236d3b208" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402620 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical points lie on the lines $u=0$ and $v=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402620 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402620 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a23b6f7f-749d-5d1a-b619-0c32cdbf023d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402621 #edb/ref 1080 "The critical points lie on the line $u=-v.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402621 #edb/